    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A superb opportunity arises to acquire this most spacious detached family home that enjoys a virtually traffic free positioning  located in a quiet yet convenient cul-de-sac.\r\n\r\nTogether with Ballybrack Shopping Centre (Anchored by Tesco)  and Cornelscourt Shopping Centre the villages of Shankill, Cabinteely, Killiney and Dalkey, Ballsbridge and Sandymount are all close at hand and combine to offer a virtually unrivaled choice of services and amenities. These include leading supermarkets, specialist retailers and numerous eateries. The area also benefits from a host of sporting and leisure clubs offering the gym, tennis, rugby, soccer swimming and GAA fans an excellent choice. \r\n\r\nThe selection of schools and educational facilities includes St Colmcille Junior National School, Scoil Chomlcille Senior National School, St Laurence College, Cabinteely Community School and Dublin College Loughlinstown.\r\n\r\nWhile there are plenty of services and amenities within walking distance, those wishing to travel further afield can avail themselves of the many frequent bus routes or the Luas Green Line (Cherrywood) which is less than 15 minutes on foot from No.10.\r\n\r\nHomes of this proportion in this cul-de-sac rarely come to market, so early viewing is essential to ensure this opportunity does not pass you by to acquire a family home that is ready to go!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Passing through the porch leads to the welcoming reception hall off which is the living / dining room. This room spans the width of the house and has two large picture windows overlooking the front garden. The kitchen can be accessed from both the hall and living / dining room, it in turn provides access to the rear garden. There is an excellent range of floor and eye units providing excellent storage and worktop space.\r\n\r\nTo the rear of the hall is the family bathroom. This has recently been upgraded and features attractive modern tiling and offers a wc, whb and a bath with shower attachments. The remaining ground floor accommodation comprises of three double bedrooms and a single bedroom that would also be an excellent study / home office.\r\n\r\nOn the first floor there is a light filled landing off which is the well-appointed shower room. The first-floor accommodation is completed by two large bedrooms each which are also suitable for numerous other uses if required."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Porch - \r\nleads to\r\n\r\nReception Hall - \r\nleads to\r\n\r\nBedroom / Study - \r\na single room.\r\n\r\nLiving / Dining Room - \r\nextends the full width of the house, open fireplace, two large picture windows.\r\n\r\nKitchen - \r\nwith fitted floor and eye level units, tiled splash back, access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\ndouble room\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\ndouble room\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\ndouble room\r\n\r\nBathroom - \r\nfully tiled and fitted with a wc, whb and a bath with shower attachments.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Landing - \r\nleads to\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\nlarge double room to the rear.\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\nlarge double room to the front.\r\n\r\nShower Room - \r\nwith decorative tiling, fitted with a wc, whb and a step in shower.\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Generously proportioned detached family home in a quiet but convenient cul de sac.\r\nWalking distance to Ballybrack Shopping Centre, Sports Clubs and public amenities\r\nOff street parking and a garage\r\nGenerous gardens to the front side and rear. \r\nExcellent transport links include public bus routes, Luas and the N11 / M50.\r\nGas fired central heating"
      },
      {
